# Was the 204-line GitHub Python template, left over from the FastAPI backend.
# It cost real time during the migration: its `lib/` entry silently kept the
# whole lib/ directory out of a commit, and `git add -A` reported nothing wrong.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*

# Next
/.next/
/out/
/build/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment. .env.sample is committed as the reference copy.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Runtime data: the SQLite database and its WAL sidecars. The directory itself
# is tracked via data/.gitkeep, so a checkout creates it owned by the user
# rather than letting Docker create it owned by root (see README).
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep

# Editors and OS. `.vscode/` and `.zed/` are one shared project setup (which
# formatter, what to keep out of search) expressed twice, because neither
# editor reads the other's directory: VS Code and Cursor take the first, Zed
# the second. They are tracked so the setup travels with the repo, and they
# have to be changed together. Anything else either editor writes into those
# directories is per-machine state and stays ignored.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
!/.vscode/launch.json
!/.vscode/extensions.json
!/.vscode/settings.json
.zed/*
!/.zed/settings.json

# Per-machine Makefile overrides, notably DEPLOY_HOST.
Makefile.local

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
